<HEAD><style>/* ============ blackwork — ink-black show reel. Palette lives in theme fields only. ============ */
.gml-card {
  --mono: var(--label-font);
  --hair: var(--neutral-border-color);
  --plate-shadow: color-mix(in srgb, var(--heading-color) 8%, transparent);
}

/* Structural geometry stays square; images become trim-filling work surfaces rather than mounted artifacts. */
.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; }

/* Signature sheet: one dominant move per working card, up to two on covers and dividers. */
.hero-surface .gml-figure,
.hero-surface .gml-figure__img,
.hero-surface img { border-radius: 0; object-fit: cover; }
.reel-lockup .gml-display,
.reel-lockup.gml-display { letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1.02; text-wrap: balance; }
.metric-mono.gml-display { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.95; }
.contact-sheet { --grid-divider-color: var(--card-color); --grid-divider-width: 3pt; --grid-seam-inset: 0; }
.contact-sheet .gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; }
.contact-sheet .gml-figure__img,
.contact-sheet img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 0; }
.credit-rail { font-family: var(--mono); border-left: 1px solid var(--hair); }
.credit-rail .gml-paragraph,
.credit-rail p { font-family: var(--mono); }
.silver-seam { --grid-divider-color: var(--hair); --grid-divider-width: 1px; --grid-seam-inset: 1em; }
.work-color .gml-figure__img,
.work-color img { border-radius: 0; }

/* Inline semantic voices. accent = ink (pair it with a real <u> mark for the index underline, the template's signature device, dose: at most one per card); muted = calm gray. */
span.textColor[data-variant='accent'] { color: var(--accent-color); }
/* The index underline itself is the editable underline mark, not decoration on the color span. */
u { text-decoration-thickness: 0.04em; text-underline-offset: 0.19em; text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent); }
span.textColor[data-variant='muted'] { color: var(--body-color-muted); }

/* ============ Data voice: monospace strictly for data (years, stats, folios, filters) ============ */
/* Mono register: class="mono" on the node (works from the wrapper or the content element). */
.mono > .gml-paragraph, p.mono, .mono p,
h1.mono, h2.mono, h3.mono, h4.mono,
.mono h1, .mono h2, .mono h3, .mono h4,
.mono > .gml-heading { font-family: var(--mono); }

/* Stat register: mono numerals over quiet captions; whitespace separation, no rules. */
.stat .gml-display, .stat [data-size], .stat h2, .stat h3 { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
.stat .gml-paragraph[data-role='caption'] { color: var(--body-color-muted); }

/* Pair hug: a caption/gloss that belongs to the block above it (rule 12b) */
.cap { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap, 13pt) * 0.4); }
/* Stat figures are tight-leaded (1.05): descenders paint outside the line box, so the gloss needs real air (T4 figure-hug). Grid cells scale --block-gap to 0.55x, hence the pt floor. */
.stat .cap { margin-block-start: max(calc(var(--block-gap, 13pt) * 0.4), 12pt); }
/* Group break: a commentary graf that must not melt into the prose above it (T4 — the cell-scaled beat sits under the wrapped-row threshold) */
.brk { margin-block-start: max(var(--block-gap, 13pt), 10.5pt); }

/* Ghost numeral voice for dividers/agenda: oversized mono, stone gray */
.folio h1, .folio h2, .folio h3, h1.folio, h2.folio, h3.folio,
.gml-display.folio, .folio [data-size] { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--palette-3); }

/* Derived index numerals (auto-renumbering markers) on the contents grid (class="idx" on the grid). */
.idx .gml-grid-cell { --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); --marker-font-size: calc(17 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-font-weight: 400; }
.idx .gml-grid-cell__marker { font-family: var(--mono); margin-right: 10pt; }

/* Ghost section numerals above each contents column (class="acts" on the grid): the folio voice, marker-driven so the strip renumbers itself. */
.acts .gml-grid-cell { --marker-color: var(--palette-3); --marker-font-size: calc(34 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-font-weight: 400; }
.acts .gml-grid-cell__marker { font-family: var(--mono); letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.3; }
/* Two extra beats between the contents heading and the strip (the recipe's heading-to-grid channel; additive over
   the native rhythm) — the marker band carries no block inset of its own, so the channel is the theme's to hold. */
.acts { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap, 13pt) * 2); }

/* Question set on the agenda spread (class="qset"): mono index numerals, marker-driven, seams instead of hand-spaced rules. */
.qset { --grid-divider-color: var(--hair); --grid-divider-width: 1px; --grid-seam-inset: 13pt; }
.qset .gml-grid-cell { --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); --marker-font-size: calc(17.5 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-font-weight: 400; }
.qset .gml-grid-cell__marker { font-family: var(--mono); margin-right: 8pt; }

/* ============ Labels: pills + the square black CTA ============ */
.gml-label { border-radius: 999px; }
.gml-label[data-variant='outline'] { outline-color: var(--hair); color: var(--body-color); }
.gml-label[data-variant='solid'] { background: var(--accent-color); color: var(--palette-4); }
.gml-label[data-variant='plain'] { color: var(--body-color-muted); }
/* CTA: square-shouldered black button (class="btn" on the solid label) */
.btn.gml-label { border-radius: 0; padding: 8pt 14pt; }

/* ============ Seams & ledgers ============ */
/* Seam clearance is a theme knob, not card padding: the renderer insets every unpainted cell from its own
   line-facing sides, so cards author no per-cell gutter padding. Prose columns beside a rule breathe wider
   than ledger rows (rule 12b seam clearance). */
.cols { --grid-divider-color: var(--hair); --grid-divider-width: 1px; --grid-seam-inset: 1.15em; }
.led { --grid-divider-color: var(--hair); --grid-divider-width: 1px; --grid-seam-inset: 0.6em; }
.proof-stack { --grid-divider-color: var(--hair); --grid-divider-width: 1px; --grid-seam-inset: 9pt; }
.gloss, .proof-copy { margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap, 13pt) * 0.45); }

/* Sharp editorial cards: hairline-bordered square cells (capabilities, tiers). CSS paint is invisible to the
   renderer, so every .cards cell authors its own even options.padding in the same change. */
/* Opaque black box over photography: the box owns its pt padding and hugs its copy. */
.overlay-paper.gml-box { padding: 18pt 20pt; --block-gap: 6pt; }
.overlay-paper.gml-box { border-radius: 0; box-shadow: 0 6pt 18pt var(--plate-shadow); }

/* ============ Work surfaces: square, flush, and unframed ============ */
.plates .gml-grid-cell { box-shadow: none; --cell-default-bg: var(--surface-color); --cell-radius: 0; }
.gallery-deep .gml-figure, .gallery-deep .gml-figure__img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
.gallery-deep .gml-figure__img { object-fit: cover; width: 100%; border-radius: 0; }

/* ============ Table: hairline project-index register ============ */
.gml-table { --table-border-color: var(--hair); --table-border-width: 1px; --table-header-bg: transparent; --table-header-color: var(--body-color-muted); --table-header-weight: 400; --table-stripe-bg: transparent; --table-radius: 0; --table-cell-padding: 8pt 10pt; }
.gml-table__row[data-header] .gml-table__cell { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: calc(10.5 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
.gml-table { border: none; }
.yearcol .gml-table__cell[data-col='0'] { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--body-color-muted); }

/* ============ Lists ============ */
li.gml-bullet::marker { content: '—\00a0\00a0'; color: var(--body-color-muted); }
li.gml-bullet.tick::marker, li.gml-bullet.tick::marker { content: '✓\00a0\00a0'; color: var(--heading-color); }

/* ============ Blockquote: bar off, bare grotesk pull quote ============ */
.gq.gml-blockquote > .gml-blockquote__bar { display: none; }
.gq.gml-blockquote { padding-inline-start: 0; }
/* The pull quote is display-adjacent type: leading tighter than body (T5) */
.gq.gml-blockquote p, .gq.gml-blockquote .gml-paragraph { line-height: 1.24; }

/* ============ Charts: quiet ink-on-paper, tabular numerals ============ */
.gml-card .gml-chart text { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

/* Graphy charts: studio-book figures — ink lead over graphite and stone, mono labels, square marks, no furniture */
.gml-chart {
  --gamma-chart-background: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-grid-color: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-border-color: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-axis-line-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--body-color) 40%, transparent);
  --gamma-chart-origin-line-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--body-color) 40%, transparent);
  --gamma-chart-font-family: var(--label-font);
  --gamma-chart-text-color: var(--body-color-muted);
  --gamma-chart-secondary-text-color: var(--body-color-muted);
  --gamma-chart-legend-background: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-legend-border-color: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-legend-item-background: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-legend-item-border: none;
  --gamma-chart-legend-item-shadow: none;
  --gamma-chart-legend-text-color: var(--heading-color);
  --gamma-chart-bar-rx: 0;
  --gamma-chart-bar-ry: 0;
  /* Series 5-8: tints of the four voices so long series stay on-register */
  --gamma-chart-line-width: 1.25px;
  --gamma-chart-line-cap: butt;
  --gamma-chart-area-opacity: 0.06;
  --gamma-chart-pie-stroke: var(--card-color);
  --gamma-chart-pie-stroke-width: 1.5px;
}

/* Rev 1: chrome-free reel. Mono survives only as evidence, not eyebrows or running furniture. */
.mono, .mono .gml-paragraph, p.mono, h2.mono, h3.mono, h4.mono { font-family: var(--mono); }
.number-top .gml-grid-cell__marker { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0; }
.capability-stack h3 { font-size: calc(28 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
.project-index .gml-table__row[data-header] .gml-table__cell { font-family: var(--body-font); font-size: calc(13.5 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--heading-color); }
.project-index-strip .gml-grid-cell { padding-top: 8pt; }

.index-code { margin-block-start: 10pt; }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Vz0tUeehWO" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/6guR-bXfHQcBbAtUgODAK.jpg" saved-media-id="jhwn9udp26b9yhi" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-abstract" alt="Abstract black-glass field shaped by one severe boundary: translucent ribbons compress through a narrow luminous opening, hard white reflections with restrained cyan and ember-red refractions, deep matte-black upper and right regions, broad calm black lower-left zone for copy, no typography or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TBsjnTH6Ti" padding="48pt 54pt 52pt"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="H5ec_jll4M" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 22pt" colspan="43"><display size="lg" class="reel-lockup">The Vow<br>of Chastity</display><p font-size="lg">Why your best work is waiting behind a rule you haven’t written yet.</p></grid-item><spacer span="17"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0MVsJdJAnQ" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid divider="sm palette-3" spacing="none" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="TGQX6h4Y7b" background-color="palette-4" padding="34pt 34pt 30pt" colspan="27"><h1 class="reel-lockup">In 1960, a publisher bet Dr. Seuss fifty dollars</h1><p>Bennett Cerf wagered $50 that Theodor Geisel could not write a book using 50 different words or fewer. Geisel agonized over the limit. <i>Green Eggs and Ham</i> was published 12 August 1960.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" vertical-sizing="hug" class="silver-seam stat"><grid-item id="jiLXuJOlrt" colspan="20"><display size="md">50</display><p role="caption" class="cap">different words or fewer</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LnrdAcUlot" colspan="20"><display size="md">49</display><p role="caption" class="cap">monosyllables</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Fv4FHvcjMA" colspan="20"><display size="md">1</display><p role="caption" class="cap">exception: “anywhere”</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.cbc.ca/lite/story/1.5686697">CBC</a> · <a href="https://brianjayjones.com/2020/08/11/sixty-years-of-green-eggs-and-ham/">Brian Jay Jones</a> · <a href="https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/green-eggs-and-ham/">Snopes</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="D80reYIqGg" class="hero-surface" padding="0" colspan="33"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/thgifJk2Ex0s4bZWbR8Z6.jpg" saved-media-id="97ts7lkkzh8ftms" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-cinematic" alt="Cinematic still of a solitary writer at a black desk arranging a tiny set of word tiles beside loose illustrated pages, warm practical light grazing hands and paper edges, objects concentrated in the upper right with deep black negative space below, no readable text, logos, branded books, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:2560,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="rbY3vxBQY3" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="40"><h2>North of 200 million copies.</h2><p>By some estimates, it became his best-selling book ever. Nobody remembers the books he wrote with unlimited vocabulary.</p></grid-item><spacer span="20"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="cy57D1cNV8" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/GDV4ncmjaBcB8gxvMvIiK.jpg" saved-media-id="99ltn6641mgplek" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-cinematic" alt="Cinematic overhead still of one pristine blank sheet isolated on a vast black worktable, a pencil and metal ruler pushed to the far edge, hard pool of light around the paper and deep surrounding shadow, bold edge crop, no readable text, logos, screens, or documents beyond the blank page" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ehEbFZ0yEg" padding="48pt 54pt 52pt"><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><spacer span="13"></spacer><grid-item id="JCqp1G5VoH" background-color="palette-4" padding="20pt 24pt" colspan="47"><display size="md" class="reel-lockup">And yet we hand people a blank page and call it a gift</display><p>Open scope. Open budget. “Surprise us.” No fixed deliverable. We treat every inherited limit as damage, when creative freedom is often just an unmade decision handed downstream.</p><p><b>The constraint is the instrument.</b></p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="EkgdFn1srE" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/YrQFYN8t0Ymt2uqONpPTa.jpg" saved-media-id="4428tdk6lom9b7j" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-abstract" alt="Abstract evidence field in matte black: hundreds of fine silver traces converge into one bright bounded corridor, thin cyan and ember-red refractions marking the edges, forceful diagonal movement with a quiet lower-left region, no typography, numbers, charts, or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Jd3uFx7GPE"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="c7efWLB79P" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 22pt" colspan="34"><p role="caption" class="mono">01</p><h1 class="reel-lockup">What the evidence actually says</h1></grid-item><spacer span="26"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="BFhlj06SG9"><grid divider="sm palette-3" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="cf6cViWwk1" class="stat" colspan="19"><display size="xl" class="reel-lockup metric-mono">111</display><h3 role="subheading">published and unpublished studies</h3><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/job.2655">Journal of Organizational Behavior · 2022 meta-analysis</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="GTKYeGo_mg" colspan="41"><h1 class="reel-lockup">111 studies disagree with your instincts</h1><p>A 2022 meta-analysis found a significant <b>positive</b> relationship between constraints and creative performance.</p><hr color="palette-3" thickness="sm"><p>The type of constraint mattered less than researchers assumed. Much of the older disagreement traced to methodology, not to the constraints themselves.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><blockquote class="gq"><p font-size="24pt">The boundary itself is doing the work.</p></blockquote></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="IkUFyDcrqn"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="3KVxgqJz81"><h1 class="reel-lockup">The finding that should annoy you most</h1><p>A Stanford study introduced a narrowing constraint during graphic-ad prototyping: a specified target audience and ad size.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><smart-layout variant="timeline" orientation="horizontal" two-sided="false" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Beginning</h4><p>The constraint arrived before prototyping.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Middle</h4><p>The constraint arrived during prototyping.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>End</h4><p><b>Late constraints produced the most novel results.</b></p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" vertical-sizing="hug" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="16rwTq_x47" colspan="42"><h3>Fixation also helped.</h3><p>A second experiment induced design fixation. Higher fixation yielded more novel results.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="dfJBy5_kqJ" colspan="18"><p role="caption"><a href="https://stacks.stanford.edu/file/druid:tf829zy3088/Zhou-BoundingCreativity.pdf">Stanford · Bounding Creativity</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Czyx0DcnGI"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="P0wHmgXWbQ"><h1 class="reel-lockup">Harder was better, even when it was worse</h1><p>In a 2023 <i>Creativity Research Journal</i> study, participants wrote short sentences under low or high constraint on the initial letters they could use.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="HkPtgcrqAq" cell-style="outline" padding="24pt" colspan="30"><p role="caption" class="mono">LOW CONSTRAINT</p><h2>More attempts succeeded.</h2><p>The task left more routes open.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7jrWvLVZGr" background-color="palette-1" padding="24pt" colspan="30"><p role="caption" class="mono">HIGH CONSTRAINT</p><h2>Fewer attempts succeeded.</h2><p>The sentences that survived were judged <b>more creative</b>.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" vertical-sizing="hug" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="ltsSJNSH_G" colspan="44"><h3>Tight rules lower your hit rate and raise your ceiling.</h3><p>Plan for more failed attempts, not fewer.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RGZuVZL48b" colspan="16"><p role="caption"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10400419.2023.2182038">Creativity Research Journal · 2023</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4o9CEOk19u"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ErHbw4dAKB"><h1 class="reel-lockup">But constraint is a dose, not a virtue</h1><p>Problem constraints and resource constraints have to be read together. One dimension alone tells you very little.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><table col-widths="[24,38,38]" header-row="true" header-col="true" borders="all" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Problem × resources</p></td><td><p>Low resource constraint</p></td><td><p>High resource constraint</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Low problem constraint</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p><b>Ambiguous opportunity</b><br>Nobody knows what the work is, so nothing gets made.</p></td><td background-color="palette-1"><p><b>Balanced</b><br>Motivation and creative search stay switched on.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>High problem constraint</p></td><td background-color="palette-1"><p><b>Balanced</b><br>Motivation and creative search stay switched on.</p></td><td background-color="palette-3"><p><b>Futile effort</b><br>Everyone knows the work and nobody can reach it.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" vertical-sizing="hug" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="x7JdFre4l3" colspan="43"><h3>The skill is tuning the limits.</h3></grid-item><grid-item id="ZtuVoXvyAZ" colspan="17"><p role="caption"><a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/20413866231202031">Organization Theory</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="uNGIt3ZpmT" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/93r_FiHKqkMWIFFBhH6qc.jpg" saved-media-id="mwlv7kuiwa2643j" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-abstract" alt="Abstract focusing mechanism in black glass: a broad field of scattered reflections bends toward one sharply illuminated aperture, silver surfaces with restrained cyan and red edge light, strong horizontal motion and calm black lower-left space, no typography or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="OA1kmkP34Y"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="VNBzKJj2s3" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 22pt" colspan="28"><p role="caption" class="mono">02</p><h1 class="reel-lockup">Why it works</h1></grid-item><spacer span="32"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="zRw47XI5Xv"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="I4oaEm2D9h"><h1 class="reel-lockup">Two kinds of rules, and only one of them helps</h1><p>Constraints can clear options away, or they can point attention toward a productive region of the problem.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="jCsPRcfsp0" cell-style="outline" padding="24pt" colspan="30"><p role="caption" class="mono">EXCLUSIONARY</p><h2>“No stock photography.”</h2><p>The rule clears the table. It tells you nothing about what belongs there instead.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EsSk4U-c7d" background-color="palette-1" padding="24pt" colspan="30"><p role="caption" class="mono">FOCUSING</p><h2>“Every image must be something a customer could have shot on their own phone.”</h2><p>The rule excludes the same options and aims the search somewhere useful.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><h3>Read your rule aloud. If it only ends arguments, rewrite it until it also starts one.</h3><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1871187122001870">Research on exclusionary and focusing constraints</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="9D7yOHntxn" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid divider="sm palette-3" spacing="none" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="U7u1FcQtDq" class="hero-surface" padding="0" colspan="32"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/S2owb6tf6gmnxvKTxkzYV.jpg" saved-media-id="sqj502nvt11qcvc" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-cinematic" alt="Cinematic still of a handheld film camera following two adult performers through a real apartment interior, practical window light, visible floor cables and unpolished walls, urgent documentary movement with deep black edge crops, no logos, readable screens, documents, or branded equipment" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:2560,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"></grid-item><grid-item id="UnZFgNB3py" background-color="palette-4" padding="32pt 34pt 28pt" colspan="28"><h1 class="reel-lockup">Filmmakers wrote theirs down and signed it</h1><p>On 13 March 1995 in Copenhagen, Lars von Trier and Thomas Vinterberg published Dogme 95 and its ten-rule “Vow of Chastity.”</p><p>Shoot on location. Record sound with the images. Keep the camera handheld. No optical work or filters. No superficial action. Here and now. <b>The director must not be credited.</b></p><blockquote class="gq"><p font-size="22pt">“Discipline is the answer... we must put our films into uniform.”</p></blockquote><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><h3>Every rule governed method. None governed meaning.</h3><p role="caption"><a href="https://as.vanderbilt.edu/koepnick/WorldCinema_f02/materials/Dogme_Manifesto.htm">Dogme 95 manifesto</a> · <a href="https://ifsstech.files.wordpress.com/2008/06/the_vow_of_chastity.pdf">Vow of Chastity</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="t7lFN-uRum" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/udyw6w1Ip37iinzw6DFG8.jpg" saved-media-id="er34qztv6uo0n3h" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-abstract" alt="Abstract vow-writing field: three sharp black-glass planes lock around an open central path, concentrated white specular edges with sparse cyan and ember-red refractions, disciplined geometry, deep shadow and a quiet lower-left copy region, no typography, documents, pens, or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="c1UTbdPAyJ"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="2hgOcsQH-X" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 22pt" colspan="31"><p role="caption" class="mono">03</p><h1 class="reel-lockup">Write your own vow</h1></grid-item><spacer span="29"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Fmjnnoxb0g"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="3meH-cSPmR"><h1 class="reel-lockup">Four steps, and you can run this on Monday</h1><p>Start with the ordinary version of the project, then remove the permission that keeps making it ordinary.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="vYq5IrQSAK" colspan="15"><h3>Name the default</h3><p>Describe the version any competent studio would make. That is the thing you are trying to escape.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="W0TJ0GgD1e" colspan="15"><h3>Find the freedom</h3><p>Identify the single permission that makes the default possible. Usually budget, stock imagery, or unlimited palette.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zDLzFk96Vx" colspan="15"><h3>Aim the hole</h3><p>Remove that permission. Turn the absence into a focusing rule that says what you must now do.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1aQuinKKow" colspan="15"><h3>Set the dose</h3><p>Write three to five rules and one condition under which you would break them.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><h3>Five rules is a vow. Fifteen is a specification, and specifications produce compliance.</h3></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="jnfz4fbZWk" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid divider="sm palette-3" spacing="none" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="bCddRH4rh0" class="hero-surface" padding="0" colspan="23"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/N4QJlopLgrNSe8VvFXyRP.jpg" saved-media-id="6jghvv7n02lcfgy" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-cinematic" alt="Cinematic still life of professional salon tools without people: silver shears, comb teeth, folded foil and a small round mirror arranged as hard graphic shapes on matte black, two-color practical lighting, bold edge crops and deep shadow, no logos, labels, readable text, products, or faces" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:2560,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="LPLj5UIz7t" background-color="palette-4" padding="16pt 18pt"><p role="caption" class="mono">FICTIONAL CONCEPT · NOT CLIENT WORK</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="YAO-l44bDx" padding="34pt 38pt 30pt" colspan="37"><h1 class="reel-lockup">Worked example: a salon rebrand that does not exist</h1><p><b>This example is invented for this talk.</b> Fenwick &amp; Pike is a fictional salon; no client commissioned it, no work was delivered, and the visuals here are concept imagery, not case-study results.</p><hr color="palette-3" thickness="sm"><h3>The default</h3><p>Soft neutral palette, serif wordmark, close-cropped model portraits, one script accent. Roughly every salon identity of the last decade.</p><h3>The load-bearing freedom</h3><p>Photography of people. Remove it and the whole default collapses.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption" class="mono">THE VOW</p><labels><label variant="outline">one typeface · two weights</label><label variant="outline">two inks · no gradients</label><label variant="outline">no photographs of people</label><label variant="outline">survive at 30mm</label></labels></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Bli5hRPhjG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="5AEGIa28jo"><h1 class="reel-lockup">What the rules forced</h1><p>Each decision arrived as a consequence of the vow.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-position="above" padding="20pt" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="681-ZAarMK" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/vMAENOCxiuTrejjVFUkM.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="comb teeth graphic mark" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The combination mark, consisting of a black comb-like figure, symbolizes the concept of comb, an everyday object used for grooming and arranging hair or other fibers.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>No people</h3><p>The identity moved toward the objects of the trade: comb teeth, foil, and the curve of a shear as flat graphic marks.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QKaC2_6OK6" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/jWQ59JLcT2SCqogs8QviBR.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="two ink print layers" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A printer icon, symbolizing the concept of printing.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Two inks</h3><p>The soft gradient look disappeared. A hard, high-contrast system could survive a photocopier and a neon sign equally.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6kngiiI9bc" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/JQCO5pLg1fr94h8Ze79f.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="small circular sticker scale test" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black square shape with rounded corners, symbolizing a sticker used for decoration or labeling.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>The 30mm rule</h3><p>It vetoed the delicate wordmark on week one. That is exactly what a good constraint does early.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="yASWph7S1U" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/VbAWcDse8Sy95PFJaZKf8R.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="single typeface hierarchy scale" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Two equal-sized scales side by side, conveying the concept of balance, harmony, and equilibrium.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>One typeface</h3><p>Hierarchy moved into scale and spacing, which is cheaper to maintain and harder to get wrong.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><h3>None of these were decisions. They were consequences.</h3></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="8TQEudkrjd"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Jv41Q14FCp"><h1 class="reel-lockup">How to tell your vow is wrong</h1><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm palette-3" marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-position="inline" padding="18pt" class="silver-seam"><grid-item id="vb0Q5AVxzu" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/7XIEFwkKEetk9idwyPou.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="prohibition sign without direction" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The sign. \n\nThe equal sign is placed centrally, indicating equality or balance within a given context.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>It only says no</h3><p>Pure prohibition is a filter, not a brief. Rewrite the rule toward the focusing form.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="GYgkV7c0ZX" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/oWedomtAtJh9ZWwq3Fm5ic.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="untouched object surviving filter" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black triangle with its tip pointing downwards, situated within a circular boundary, embodying the concept of filtering or selection.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Nothing has died yet</h3><p>If two weeks in nothing you liked has been vetoed, the rules are decorative.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="N-ss06Wrtj" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/WC7cTPNS7LJ9CUSY54un.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="speech censored by rigid frame" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A four-sided shape with four right angles, forming a basic structural outline, symbolizing the concept of a frame.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>It governs meaning</h3><p>Method rules are generative. Rules about what the work may <i>say</i> are censorship in a better outfit.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NANpiGXWIC" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Wn7AhS2ngGpoW8sE6Irf.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="overloaded team blocked path" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Three interconnected shapes/forms, often symbolizing collaboration, unity, or cooperation among individuals working together towards a common goal.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Nothing ships</h3><p>Everyone is miserable and the work stalls. Loosen one dimension instead of pushing harder.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">Constraint dose: <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/20413866231202031">Organization Theory</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="xLt41OSj-s" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/g_M7i5lFbJUlnb478LIIt.jpg" saved-media-id="smzd7pg7lqo0r3b" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="reel-abstract" alt="Abstract black-glass closing field: one luminous ribbon is deliberately cut away, forcing the remaining silver, cyan and ember-red reflections into an unexpected new path, sweeping motion across the upper and right frame with a calm matte-black lower-left third for copy, no typography or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SDENZB256j" padding="48pt 54pt 52pt"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="7oW3b_6Dyy" background-color="palette-4" padding="20pt 24pt" colspan="47"><display size="md" class="reel-lockup">Pick the freedom you’re most afraid to lose</display><p>The evidence points one way: constraints predict better creative performance, late ones especially, and the real work is tuning the dose rather than defending every option.</p><p>Find the permission you would defend hardest in a meeting. Take it away for two weeks and write down what happens.</p><p><b>Bennett Cerf’s fifty dollars bought the best-selling thing Geisel ever made. Your version costs less than that.</b></p></grid-item><spacer span="13"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>